<%# Profile header — Hoojah 2026 (redesign Phase 4, Task 4.4), mockup ~1388-1408.
    Root carries `dom_id(user, :profile_header)` so update.turbo_stream.erb can
    replace just this block after an edit. Locals: user.

    Faithful port of the legacy SPA `UserProfile.jsx` header column (avatar, name,
    @handle, headline, optional location + link, follow control, follower/
    following counts), now on the `.profile-hero` gradient treatment
    (`linear-gradient(160deg, var(--primary), #5b74f0)`, app/assets/tailwind/
    application.css `@layer components`, same family as `.trending-hero` /
    `.verdict-hero`) instead of flat `bg-primary`. `_gated_header` deliberately
    stays on flat `bg-primary` — Gate 4's private-account whitelist is not this
    partial's concern and is not touched here.

    ACTION BAR (new this task): back / share / settings-gear, mockup's
    icon row above the avatar. The gear is the OWNER-ONLY trigger for the
    existing `_profile_edit` `<dialog>` (Slice 9, Task 4.6) — that dialog is
    UNCHANGED in substance, only its trigger icon (pencil → gear, matching the
    mockup) and its position (absolute top-right corner → inline in this row)
    moved; see the header comment on `_profile_edit` for the full note. Back
    goes to the main feed — there is no "previous screen" concept server-side to
    return to, so `root_path` is the one destination that is always valid. Share
    reuses the SAME `share` Stimulus controller + `ui/_menu` idiom as
    `hujahs/_share_menu` (Web Share API on capable devices, six real `<a href>`
    fallback rows otherwise — no JS required), pointed at the profile's own URL
    instead of a hoojah's.

    AVATAR: `variant: :tile` (Hoojah 2026's gradient-initials TREATMENT), same
    choice `debates/_verdict` and `debates/_debate_pending` already make for an
    avatar rendered ON a coloured hero — see `ui/_avatar`'s header comment: tile
    is "for surfaces that want the tile look on purpose, not merely as a
    fallback." `border-2 border-white/50` is the mockup's translucent ring.

    FOLLOW: `render "follow_button", user:, surface: :gradient` — the surface
    local `_follow_button` gained in Phase 2.4 for exactly this hero. It already
    renders BOTH the Follow/Following pill AND the secondary Block control as a
    pair; nothing extra is added here for a "round secondary button" — that IS
    the Block control the partial already renders on `:gradient`.

    BADGES: `bg-white/18` (2026 token; was `bg-white/20` pre-redesign) — no
    light-background variant exists, per `BadgeChip.prompt.md`.

    FOLLOWER/FOLLOWING COUNTS: kept at the foot of the hero, unstyled changes
    aside from the surrounding redesign — Task 4.4's mockup slice doesn't show
    them, but dropping the only on-page links to `/u/:username/followers` and
    `/u/:username/following` would be a real navigation regression, not a scoped
    omission like the count TABS (Hoojahs/Responses/Debates — a SEPARATE next
    task, per this task's brief). Do not confuse the two.

    FROZEN: `dom_id(user, :profile_header)` is what `users/update.turbo_stream.erb`
    replaces after a profile edit, and what `_gated_header` deliberately mirrors. %>
<% owner = user_signed_in? && current_user.id == user.id %>
<% profile_share_url = profile_url(user.username) %>
<% profile_share_text = "@#{user.username} on Hoojah" %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(user, :profile_header) %>" class="w-full profile-hero flex flex-col">
  <%# Action bar: back / share / settings (owner only). %>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-2 pt-2">
    <%= link_to root_path, class: "flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full text-white no-underline", aria: {label: "Back"} do %>
      <%= lucide_icon("arrow-left", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
    <% end %>
    <div class="flex items-center">
      <details class="relative shrink-0"
               data-controller="share"
               data-share-title-value="Hoojah profile"
               data-share-text-value="<%= profile_share_text %>"
               data-share-url-value="<%= profile_share_url %>">
        <summary class="list-none cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full text-white" aria-label="Share this profile">
          <%= lucide_icon("share-2", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
        </summary>
        <%= render layout: "ui/menu", locals: {width: "w-52"} do %>
          <h6 class="text-xs text-grey px-3 pb-1">Share this profile via</h6>
          <button type="button" hidden
                  data-share-target="button"
                  data-action="share#share"
                  class="<%= ds_menu_item_classes %> border-0 bg-transparent cursor-pointer">
            Share…
          </button>
          <%= link_to "WhatsApp", "https://wa.me/?text=#{CGI.escape("#{profile_share_text} #{profile_share_url}")}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
          <%= link_to "X", "https://x.com/intent/tweet?url=#{CGI.escape(profile_share_url)}&text=#{CGI.escape(profile_share_text)}&via=hoojah_my", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
          <%= link_to "Telegram", "https://t.me/share/url?url=#{CGI.escape(profile_share_url)}&text=#{CGI.escape(profile_share_text)}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
          <%= link_to "Facebook", "https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=#{CGI.escape(profile_share_url)}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
          <%= mail_to "hello@rudzainy.com", "Email", subject: "Hoojah profile", body: "#{profile_share_text}\n\n#{profile_share_url}", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
        <% end %>
      </details>
      <% if owner %>
        <%= render "profile_edit", user: user, wrapper_class: "shrink-0", open: local_assigns.fetch(:edit_open, false) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-col items-center px-4 pb-6">
    <%= render "ui/avatar", user: user, size: :lg, variant: :tile, class: "mb-3 border-2 border-white/50" %>
    <h5 class="mb-0 text-lg font-extrabold"><%= user.full_name %></h5>
    <div class="text-sm opacity-85">@<%= user.username %></div>

    <% if user.headline.present? %>
      <div class="mt-2 text-center text-sm opacity-95 max-w-xs"><%= user.headline %></div>
    <% end %>

    <% if user.location.present? || user.link.present? %>
      <div class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-3.5 text-xs opacity-90">
        <% if user.location.present? %>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1">
            <%= lucide_icon("map-pin", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %> <%= user.location %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
        <% if user.link.present? %>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1">
            <%= lucide_icon("globe", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %>
            <%= link_to user.link, user.link, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener nofollow", class: "text-white underline" %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="mt-3.5">
      <%= render "follow_button", user: user, surface: :gradient %>
    </div>

    <% if user.badges.any? %>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
        <% user.badges.each do |badge| %>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold bg-white/18 rounded-full px-2.5 py-1.5"
                title="<%= badge[:description] %>">
            <%= lucide_icon(badge[:icon], class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %>
            <%= badge[:name] %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="mt-4 text-sm flex items-center gap-1 opacity-90">
      <%= link_to user_followers_path(user.username), class: "flex items-center gap-1 text-white no-underline" do %>
        <%= render "follower_count", user: user %>
      <% end %>
      <span class="mx-2">·</span>
      <%= link_to user_following_path(user.username), class: "flex items-center gap-1 text-white no-underline" do %>
        <%= lucide_icon("user-plus", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
        <span><%= user.following.size %></span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
